			"Charges: test mode, a change of its look out of combat and /flatui charges show the sample in the new look; with \001Spell art\002, Maelstrom Weapon gaining a stack each second up to 5, also when test mode is already on as you pick it.",
			"New \001Bar art\002 row on the \001Experience and menu bars\002 page (\001Flat fill\002 by default). \001The game's modern art\002 draws Flat UI's experience and reputation bars with the game's own modern fills on its dark bar background, in place of \001Bar texture\002, \001Experience colour\002 and the standing colours. Experience is the purple fill, and the blue rested fill while you are rested. Reputation takes the red, orange, yellow, green or blue fill of its standing. The tooltip, the quest stretch, the gains, the level flash and the text work on top as before, and test mode's sample bar uses the art too. \001Bar background\002 off leaves out the dark background. Where the game has no such art, the bar keeps its flat fill and /flatui status says so.",
			"Text around the map: each place row (\001Coordinates place\002, \001Durability place\002, \001Frame rate place\002, \001Time place\002) now also offers \001On the map, at the bottom\002. The line sits just inside the map's bottom edge, outlined so it reads over the ground, with its tooltip, click and light under the mouse as before. On a round map it is raised to stay inside the circle. Lines there stack upward and take no room under the map, so the addon button row and the zone name keep their place.",
			"Text around the map: a line that comes into view, such as the coordinates as you leave a dungeon, durability at 50% or a test mode sample, now fades in over 0.15 seconds instead of popping on. Hiding stays instant, so the lines below close up at once.",
			"Minimap: where the game refuses the square mask and the map keeps its round one, the name of who pinged now stays inside the round edge. Before, it was kept inside a square there and could sit outside the circle.",
			"\001Quest count\002: with \001Quests ready in the count\002 on, pointing at the count now lists up to five of the quests ready to hand in by name, in \001Quest colour\002 (\"Kobold Camp Cleanup\"), then \"and 2 more\", above the click hint. The list stays up to date while they point at it.",
			"/flatui hide tracker (or minimap, buffs, objective tracker, or any row's name or part of it) now hides that frame or shows it again, from chat or a macro, and says which: \"Flat UI: Objective tracker is hidden. /flatui hide tracker shows it again.\" or \"Flat UI: Objective tracker shows again.\". In a fight the change waits for its end. /flatui hide list names the frames that are hidden. A plain /flatui hide still opens the \001Hidden frames\002 page.",
			"\001/flatui move\002: with several boxes selected, a new \001Hide these\002 button beside \001Reset these\002 hides every selected frame that has a row on the \001Hidden frames\002 page. It reads \001Show these\002 once all of them are hidden, and is dimmed when none of them has a row. Chat names once any selected frame without a row: \"Flat UI: Chat has no row on the Hidden frames page, so it stays.\"",
			"\001/flatui move\002: Ctrl-A now selects every box that can move, including boxes behind the toolbar or the inspector. That is every shown box except those of frames the game places and those hidden with their eye in the frame list. The inspector reads \"24 frames selected\", and the arrow keys, the align buttons and \001Reset these\002 work on them all. Escape lets go as before. The \001Frame list\002 tooltip mentions it.",
			"With \001Error text size\002 or \001Zone title size\002 away from 100%, a new font picked on the \001Fonts\002 page now reaches the red error text, the yellow quest lines and the zone titles at once, at their size. Before, they kept the old face until a /reload.",
			"The hit table no longer catches the mouse once it fades out in a fight (the target dies, they drop it, or \001Show\002 hides it): enemies and the world behind that spot get their mouseover and tooltip again at once. A table that first shows during a fight now shows its own tooltip with \001Tooltip when you point at it\002.",
			"New \001Raid marker on the name\002 (on): a unit's tooltip shows the skull, moon or other raid marker it carries as a small icon before its name, under \001Unit colours\002 on the \001Tooltips\002 page.",
			"New \001Away and busy after the name\002 (on): a player who is away or busy has a dim <AFK> or <DND> after their name on their tooltip, as \"Mara <AFK>\".",
			"New \001Flash the game's icon when you are named\002 (on), under \001Mentions\002 on the \001Chat text\002 page: while the game is in the background, its icon on the taskbar or dock flashes for a line that names them, as it does for a whisper, at most once every 10 seconds.",
			"\001Show recent chat after a reload\002: each name in the restored lines is now a player link, in its class colour where the game knows it, so a click whispers and a right-click opens the player menu as on a live line. \001Copy recent chat\002 still copies plain [Name].",
			"\001Duration format\002 \001Minutes and seconds (28:41)\002: a buff of an hour or more now reads as hours and minutes, as 1h42 or 1h05, down to 59:59, in place of 2h, then 90m to 60m. Test mode's samples match.",
			"The \001Copy recent chat\002 box and the web address box now fade in with the game's window sounds, play the closing sound as they shut, and have a small cross at the top right that lights under the mouse and closes the box.",
			"\001Carrot on a Stick while riding\002: the trinket it replaced is now kept for each character, so it goes back on as they get off after a /reload or a disconnect during the ride too.",
			"\001Queue line on trinket tooltips\002 no longer shows on the rows of the \001Trinket queue\002 window, which show the same already. It still shows on trinkets in the bags and on the Character window.",
			"Consumables bar: a button now lights up under the mouse with an accent border and a soft white wash. While its key or the mouse button is held it darkens and sinks a pixel, so every use of the bar is felt.",
			"Consumables bar: an oil, sharpening stone, weightstone or poison now goes straight onto your weapon. A click puts it on your main hand and a right-click on a weapon in your off hand, with no glowing hand to aim, as the tooltip says (\"Click: on your main hand. Right-click: on your off hand.\"). Shift+right-click still puts it on your list or takes it off.",
			"Consumables bar: an elixir, flask or scroll whose buff is on you now has a green border and the minutes left at its top right, as \"14m\". It goes plain again as the buff runs out, so a missing buff stands out.",
			"Consumables bar: the tooltip of an item that is cooling down now says \"Ready in 1:42\" in warm text and counts down while the mouse stays. It says \"Ready\" in green as the cooldown ends.",
			"Consumables bar: \001Show count\002 now shows a count of 3 or fewer in amber, so the last few flasks stand out before the red 0. The count goes white again after a restock.",
			"Data panels: the invisible click area of the \001Hearthstone\002 slot now goes with its panel. Before, turning the panel or the page off in a fight, or the page stopping on an error in one, left a click area there after the fight that could use the Hearthstone.",
			"World and cursor: with nothing glowing near you, ticking \001Glow on the nearest object\002 or changing \001Glow colour\002 or \001Glow size\002 out of a fight with the options window open now shows the glow for 3 seconds a little above the middle of the screen, at its new size. With \001By what it is\002 it steps through green, copper, gold and white.",
